Z||000006||JetroGT||11-02-2001||04:58 AM||||I just fixed it. Well I put a band-aid on it anyway. It was G400, groun 400. It's the common ground for the tail light harness. I guess it's located under the rear clip on the right side. My car is a Wisconsin car so it has lots of rust. I guess the ground finally rusted away compleatly. To fix it I spliced into my right side reverse ground wire and ran it to the bumper support. Or whatever that galvinized piece is. It's just a wrap around tape up job. I'll fix it for real next week with solder and actaully drill a hole for the bolt. I wedged it between the two pieces of metal..||||reg||1
